{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome in each lottery and prefers the lottery that includes a sure (i.e., 100% certain) outcome. A sure outcome means an outcome that occurs with probability 1. In Lottery A, the outcomes are 6000 Euros with 25% and 0 Euros with 75% — there is no outcome that occurs with 100% probability. In Lottery B, the outcomes are 4000 with 25%, 2000 with 25%, and 0 with 50% — also no outcome occurs with 100% probability. Therefore, neither lottery contains a sure outcome. The decision reason would thus be indifferent between A and B, or not applicable, since neither lottery satisfies the condition of having a sure outcome. The relevant information for the reason — presence of a sure outcome — is absent in both lotteries.",
